{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"The Exterior as Not-Self","html":"<article id='sn35.227'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Saṁyutta Nikāya 35.227 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Linked Discourses 35.227 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>17. Saṭṭhipeyyālavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>17. Sixty Abbreviated Texts </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Bāhirāyatanaanattasutta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Exterior as Not-Self </span></h1></header>\n<p><span class='root'>“Rūpā, bhikkhave, anattā. Saddā … gandhā … rasā … phoṭṭhabbā … dhammā anattā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“Mendicants, sights, sounds, smells, tastes, touches, and ideas are not-self. </span></p>\n<p><span class='root'>Evaṁ passaṁ …pe… </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Seeing this … </span>\n<span class='root'>nāparaṁ itthattāyāti pajānātī”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>They understand: ‘… there is nothing further for this place.’” </span></p>\n<p class='endvagga'><span class='root'>Saṭṭhipeyyālo samatto. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<p class='uddana-intro'><span class='root'>Tassuddānaṁ </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<blockquote class='uddanagatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Chandenaṭṭhārasa honti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>atītena ca dve nava; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yadaniccāṭṭhārasa vuttā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>tayo ajjhattabāhirā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Peyyālo saṭṭhiko vutto, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>buddhenādiccabandhunāti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endkanda'><span class='root'>Suttantāni saṭṭhi. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
